 "tier1Summary": "The UN's 35-year [[p:United Nations Mission for the Referendum in Western Sahara|Western Sahara mission]] ended after a Russian veto. Morocco says the ceasefire holds, while the [[p:Polisario Front|Polisario]] warns of war. Sudan and Ethiopia expelled each other's diplomats over RSF drones that Khartoum says are launched from Ethiopian soil, as UN officials warn of a campaign against Sudan's power and fuel infrastructure. Ebola has now killed more than 5,300 people, and vaccine trials are starting. Fighting persists in Tigray, and Mekelle is under curfew. South Africa awaits local election results on Sunday.\n\nElsewhere, Qatar is pushing a US–Iran interim deal after US strikes on Qeshm, and Iran says mines damaged tankers in Hormuz. [[p:Donald Trump]] met Russia's [[p:Kirill Dmitriev]] ahead of the Abu Dhabi talks, and Russia's bombing of Komyshuvakha killed at least 43.",
